                <pb facs="0346" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">175.1/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cobb</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-15T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your August 11, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>You may inform High Commission that until Allied Treaty with Turkey is ratified
                    and an agreement between the United States and Great Britain regarding
                    recognition of British mandate in Palestine is arrived at the Department trusts
                    that the terms of the arrangement between the British Legal Secretary and your
                    office will be followed.</p>
                <p>The Department is taking the matter up with London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
